            <ArticleTitle>Bivalirudin use during PCI for stent thrombosis in a patient with subacute intracranial hemorrhage.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>136-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Caring for patients at high risk is inherent to the practice of interventional cardiology. Recognizing high-risk situations, minimizing risk and employing preventive techniques proactively to avoid complications cannot be over-emphasized within this dynamic field. This case demonstrates real-world concerns and decision-making regarding severe bleeding risk, rescue angioplasty, stent thrombosis, appropriate usage of intravascular ultrasound and differences in stent design. Three take-home messages are identified to reduce complications in similar situations.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
